pan\n1079\tokada-s@jaist.ac.jp\n1080\t\n1081\tCCS Concepts\n1082\t• Human-centered computing → Empirical studies in collaborative and social computing; • Applied computing →\n1083\tPsychology; • Computing methodologies → Natural language\n1084\tprocessing.\n1085\t\n1086\tKeywords\n1087\tinterpersonal attraction; speed dating; large language models;\n1088\tspeech processing; multimodal fusion\n1089\tACM Reference Format:\n1090\tYuriko Kikuchi, Takato Hayashi, Ryusei Kimura, Naoya Inoue, Ryo Ishii,\n1091\tand Shogo Okada. 2026. Supplementary Appendix to: Speech Signals Complement LLMs for Predicting Interpersonal Attraction in Speed Dating. In\n1092\tINTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON MULTIMODAL INTERACTION (ICMI\n1093\t’26), October 05–09, 2026, Napoli, Italy. ACM, New York, NY, USA, 7 pages.\n1094\thttps://doi.org/10.1145/3776574.3831151\n1095\t\n1096\tThroughout this appendix, F2M denotes female participants rating\n1097\tmale partners, and M2F denotes male participants rating female\n1098\tpartners; the direction runs from the rater to the rated partner. Section, table, and figure numbers use S as the supplementary prefix.\n1099\tWithin table and figure condition labels, S1 and S2 denote Session 1\n1100\t(nominally 5 minutes) and Session 2 (nominally 10 minutes), respectively. Unless otherwise stated, Claude denotes the prespecified\n1101\ttranscript-only LLM used in the primary analysis, Claude Sonnet 4.6\n1102\twith extended thinking disabled; HuBERT denotes the supervised\n1103\tspeech predictor built on frozen HuBERT-Large representations.\n1104\tThe main fusion is their weighted score-level late fusion. Claude\n1105\t(thinking) denotes the auxiliary Claude configuration with extended\n1106\tthinking enabled. Here, LLM denotes a large language model and\n1107\tMLLM denotes a multimodal LLM. Bare LLM/LLMs refer to the\n1108\tmodel class or a set of candidate models, not to Claude as a fixed\n1109\tshorthand.\n1110\t\n1111\tThis work is licensed under a Creative Common